<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela gov't requests $2 bln spending credit.</title>
<headline>Venezuela gov't requests $2 bln spending credit.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's cabinet approved Wednesday a 902 billion bolivar ($1.9 billion) spending request to finance public sector wage rises, Information Minister Fernando Egana said.</p>
<p>The unbudgeted request still has to be approved by Congress.</p>
<p>&quot;The credit will be financed by oil revenues via a newly revised tax declaration by PdVSA worth 638 billion bolivars,&quot; Egana told reporters.</p>
<p>The spending will also be backed by revenues from a gasoline sales tax, worth 57 billion bolivars, and extraordinary oil revenues worth some 200 billion bolivars, Egana added.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
